V1:
    atmospheric model is upto a certain point post which drag effects taper off, so I have used a general exponential taper 

    Interpolation formula used for both ISP and thrust:
    basically using a ratio of current pressure and pressure at sea level to determine state between vaccum and sea level:
    ie:
        if ratio is 1, then sea level values, and if ratio is 0 then vaccum values. 

    S is a list of the current state at all points, when passed through the derivative() functtion it returns d which is a list of all the different rates of change

    Instead of Euler's method for integration, I've applied a method called Rk4 for more accuracy.
    RK4:
        -Eulers method assumes that there is no change in between the time step chosen, it just extends the straight tangent line at that point for the whole timestep
        -Rk4 computes the slope at 4 different points throughout the time step and uses an average slope for more accurate results

V2:
    function get angle uses an angle theta that is linearly increased as t grows larger up till max angle is achieved at 

    derivative functions now consider x, vx and vy 

    horizontal velocity addition helps get into orbit 

V3: 
    Objective: Refine pitch maneuver 
    Changes:
        - New coordinate system using v and gamma(angle between velocity and local horizontal) Instead of vy, vx
        - Forces split along tangential and normal components to the velocity vector, where the normal component causes rotation
        - during thrust, a commanded angle is added which is slightly different from gamma (smaller), this mismatch between the angles
        creates a component of thrust along velocity and one perp. (happens during pitch)
        - post pitch, gamma and commanded angle are same so thrust is in the direction of velocity.

V4:
    Objective: Add MECO(main engine cut off) 
    Changes:
        -A simple check to see once Propellant one is over
        -Dry mass one(9 merlon engines, empty fuel tanks, etc..) is seperated
        -Rocket continues with the thrust of one merlin engine and propellant 2.

    Issue:
        -No orbital insertion, rocket continues until propellant is exhausted.
    
V5:
    Objective: Add Orbital mechanics/SECO
    Changes:
        -Calculates Orbital mechanics values for every timestep after stage 2 begins
        -checks if orbit is valid: SOE<0, perigee altitude > 150km 
        -tuned kick angle slightly to achieve better gamma values
        -plot MECO and SECO points seperately
    nuances:
        -Gamma value tends to go negative by the end, happens because integration loop keeps going causing post apogee downward arc values to get recorded

V6:
    Polar coordinates, Orbit visualisation, Code revamp
    Changes:
        * curvature term  +(v cos gamma)/r  in dgamma/dt        (spherical Earth)
        * polar angle phi integrated as a state variable        (replaces flat-Earth x)
        * payload + fairing mass; get_thrust keyed on stage, not on absolute mass
        * 4 g throttle cap
        * closed-loop pitch guidance on stage 2 (altitude -> vertical speed -> gamma)
        * engine cutoff located exactly by bisection on the final RK4 step
        * full orbital-element set + insertion report
        * orbit visualisation with an analytic conic overlaid on the integrated arc
